# Git decides binary-vs-text by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8000
# bytes. A PDF written without stream compression can contain none at all,
# so git stores it as text: GitHub then tries to render it as source, and
# any end-of-line conversion silently corrupts it. Declare the types
# explicitly rather than relying on that guess.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary

# Source files keep LF in the repository regardless of the checkout platform.
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
